---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Hi, I’m Jorge Benavides Aspiazu</h1>

			<p>
				I work across the full stack of connected systems: embedded firmware and
				hardware constraints, LPWAN and satellite networks, data ingestion pipelines,
				cloud backends, and the intelligence layer that reads what those systems produce.
			</p>

			<p>
				This site is a notebook of engineering problems that only show up once systems
				grow — especially at the boundaries between devices, networks, and the cloud —
				and the trade-offs that survive real production use.
			</p>

			<p>
				<strong>Start here:</strong>
				<a href="/blog/does-ai-fit-into-the-iot-stack/">
				Does AI fit into the IoT stack?
				</a>
			</p>

			<p>
				I work with teams on existing IoT systems — architecture reviews, multi-network
				integrations, and diagnosing hard-to-debug production issues.
			</p>

			<p>
				Most engagements start as focused technical work and often expand into broader
				system design or implementation support as complexity grows.
			</p>

			<p>
				Typical areas I work on include:
			</p>

			<ul>
				<li>Embedded and hardware-constrained systems</li>
				<li>LPWAN and satellite network integrations</li>
				<li>Device lifecycle, presence, and control-plane design</li>
				<li>Data ingestion pipelines and production observability</li>
				<li>AI intelligence layers over IoT pipelines</li>
			</ul>
			</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
